<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-02--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-memory-02: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.09";
    dc:description "This is a conceptual answer to a paradox about what makes an individual or a lineage persist. Molecular, developmental, and phylogenetic records describe change, but they do not contain a result that would confirm or refute confabulation as the resolution. The claim has no empirical decision criterion.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The persistence paradox is a philosophical tension about identity through change. No biological variable distinguishes continuous adaptive confabulation as its resolution from other accounts of development and lineage continuity.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Any observed physiological change can be narrated as confabulation or as ordinary turnover.", "Identity through change is not a measured variable.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.85"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.088"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-02--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
